.TH START-DAQ.SH 1 "2026-09-10" "mu2edaq-shifter-tools" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
start-daq.sh \- start the Mu2e DAQ for one partition in tmux
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B start-daq.sh
[\fB\-c\fR \fIconfig\fR]
[\fB\-z\fR \fIpartition\fR]
[\fB\-e\fR \fIenvironment\fR]
[\fB\-a\fR]
[\fB\-n\fR]
[\fB\-h\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B start-daq.sh
brings up one DAQ partition. It creates a tmux session named
\fBdaq\-\fIpartition\fR whose first window is a plain shell for the
operator, then adds one window per active environment. Each of those
windows sources
.BR setup-online.sh (1)
for its environment and runs \fBots\fR, dropping to an interactive
shell when \fBots\fR exits so the window survives for inspection.
.PP
Windows are named \fBdaq\-\fIpartition\fB\-\fIenvironment\fR.
.BR stop-daq.sh (1)
addresses them by that name, so the two commands do not have to agree
on a window ordering.
.PP
The set of environments to start comes from the partition's
\fBactive_environments\fR list in the operations YAML, unless
overridden with one or more \fB\-e\fR options.
.PP
The Python virtual environment that
.BR daq-read-config (1)
needs is created automatically by running
.BR bootstrap.sh (1)
if it is missing, so a fresh checkout can be started with no other
preparation.
.PP
Starting a partition that already has a tmux session is refused; stop
it first.
.SH OPTIONS
Configuration precedence is command line, then environment variable,
then .env file, then config file, then built-in default.
.TP
.BR \-c ", " \-\-config " " \fIFILE\fR
Operations YAML to read. Environment: \fBMU2EDAQ_CONFIG\fR. Default:
the first \fIdaq\-operations.yaml\fR on the config search path (see
.BR daq-read-config (1)).
.TP
.BR \-z ", " \-\-partition " " \fINAME\fR
Partition to start. Environment: \fBMU2EDAQ_PARTITION\fR. Default:
\fIpartition_0\fR.
.TP
.BR \-e ", " \-\-environment " " \fINAME\fR
Start only this environment instead of the partition's active list.
May be given more than once.
.TP
.BR \-a ", " \-\-attach
Attach to the tmux session once every window has been created.
.TP
.BR \-n ", " \-\-dry\-run
Print the tmux commands that would be run and exit without starting
anything.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Show a usage summary and exit.
.TP
.B \-\-debug
Trace execution with \fBset \-x\fR.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B START_DAQ_SH_OPTS
Extra options, prepended to the command line. \fBSTART_DAQ_OPTS\fR is
also accepted for compatibility with the pre-rename script, and is
used only when \fBSTART_DAQ_SH_OPTS\fR is unset.
.TP
.B MU2EDAQ_ROOT
Installation root, if it cannot be found by walking up from the
script. Recorded in \fI~/.mu2edaq/env\fR by
.BR install-login.sh (1).
.SH FILES
.TP
.I config/daq-operations.yaml
Partition and environment definitions.
.TP
.I ~/.mu2edaq/env
Recorded installation root.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
The session was created, or the dry run completed.
.TP
.B 1
tmux is missing, the configuration could not be read, the partition has
no active environments, or its session already exists.
.TP
.B 2
A command line option was not recognised.
.SH EXAMPLES
Start the default partition and attach to it:
.PP
.RS
.nf
start-daq.sh -a
.fi
.RE
.PP
Start only the tracker environment of \fIpartition_1\fR, using an
explicit config:
.PP
.RS
.nf
start-daq.sh -c ~/my-ops.yaml -z partition_1 -e tracker
.fi
.RE
.PP
See what would happen without touching tmux:
.PP
.RS
.nf
start-daq.sh -n -z partition_0
.fi
.RE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR stop-daq.sh (1),
.BR daq-status.sh (1),
.BR setup-online.sh (1),
.BR create-environment.sh (1),
.BR daq-read-config (1),
.BR bootstrap.sh (1),
.BR tmux (1)
